  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 79-year-old man is brought to the emergency department after his second fall at home in the past month. He sustained no significant injury on this occasion. He lives alone, takes five regular medications, and his family are concerned about his safety at home.',
  'What is the most appropriate next step in his management?',
  array['falls assessment','multifactorial risk assessment']
),
('c9000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000023', 'ukmla', '8738215b-5827-41b4-9a98-8a28e23f8453',
  'draft', 'core',
  'An 84-year-old woman is assessed in a falls clinic. She has lost 5 kg unintentionally over the past year, describes feeling exhausted most days, walks slowly, and her grip strength is measurably reduced on dynamometry. She has had two falls in the past six months and low physical activity levels.',
  'Which geriatric syndrome does this presentation most likely represent?',
  array['frailty','sarcopenia']
),
