  'draft', 'core',
  'A 77-year-old man on a medical ward round is noted to be taking amlodipine, bendroflumethiazide, zopiclone, and amitriptyline for neuropathic pain. He has had two falls on the ward in the past week, both unwitnessed, with no significant injury. His observations and blood glucose are normal.',
  'What is the most appropriate initial step in reducing his falls risk?',
  array['polypharmacy','falls','medication review']
),
('c9000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000025', 'ukmla', '8738215b-5827-41b4-9a98-8a28e23f8453',
  'draft', 'core',
  'A 75-year-old man describes recurrent episodes of sudden collapse without clear warning, occasionally associated with brief loss of consciousness, some occurring while turning his head to look over his shoulder while driving. He has carotid sinus tenderness and reproducible bradycardia and hypotension on carotid sinus massage under ECG monitoring.',
  'What is the most likely diagnosis?',
  array['carotid sinus hypersensitivity','cardiovascular syncope','falls']
),
('c9000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000026', 'ukmla', '8738215b-5827-41b4-9a98-8a28e23f8453',
  'draft', 'foundation',
  'An 82-year-old woman who lives alone and rarely goes outdoors is found to have low mood, generalised bone and muscle aches, and proximal muscle weakness making it difficult for her to rise from a chair. Blood tests show low serum 25-hydroxyvitamin D, mildly low calcium, and raised alkaline phosphatase.',
  'What is the most likely underlying cause of her symptoms and falls risk?',
  array['vitamin D deficiency','osteomalacia','falls']
),
