  'draft', 'core',
  'An 86-year-old woman on warfarin for atrial fibrillation falls at home and sustains a minor laceration to her scalp. She did not lose consciousness and has no focal neurological deficit, but her daughter is concerned because she takes warfarin and her last INR was 3.2.',
  'What is the most appropriate immediate management?',
  array['anticoagulation','head injury','falls']
),
