  'draft', 'core',
  'A 66-year-old woman has been taking oral alendronic acid for osteoporosis for the past five years. She now presents with several weeks of dull thigh pain, and an X-ray shows a transverse fracture with a characteristic lateral cortical thickening ("beaking") of the femoral shaft.',
  'What is the most likely explanation for this finding?',
  array['atypical femoral fracture','bisphosphonate complication']
),
