  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 76-year-old woman sustains a distal radius (wrist) fracture after a fall from standing height. This is her first fragility fracture. She is otherwise well and has no other risk factors identified.',
  'What is the most appropriate next step in her ongoing care?',
  array['fracture liaison service','secondary fracture prevention']
),
('c9000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000041', 'ukmla', '9b7d33c2-47ca-4e44-b461-41e1542edc0a',
  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 83-year-old woman with no history of reflux or peptic ulcer disease has been taking omeprazole 20 mg daily for the past six years, started during a hospital admission for an unrelated reason and never reviewed since. She takes no NSAIDs and has no current gastrointestinal symptoms.',
  'What is the most appropriate approach to her omeprazole?',
  array['deprescribing','PPI','STOPP criteria']
),
