  'draft', 'core',
  'An 86-year-old woman presents with new confusion, dry mouth, blurred vision, and constipation. Her regular medications include amitriptyline for neuropathic pain, oxybutynin for overactive bladder, and chlorphenamine for seasonal allergies, all started separately by different prescribers over recent years.',
  'What is the most likely explanation for her presentation?',
  array['anticholinergic burden','polypharmacy','delirium']
),
