  'draft', 'core',
  'An 81-year-old man with hypertension and chronic kidney disease (baseline eGFR 45 mL/min/1.73m2) is taking ramipril and furosemide. He is started on ibuprofen by a locum GP for knee osteoarthritis. One week later he presents unwell with reduced urine output, and blood tests show eGFR has fallen to 18 mL/min/1.73m2 with a significantly raised creatinine.',
  'What is the most likely cause of his acute kidney injury?',
  array['NSAID nephrotoxicity','triple whammy','AKI']
),
